# Frontend Angular — Mobile-first & MBV2 conventions

## Screen priority

Design **mobile → tablet → desktop**. Always start with a small viewport (320–390px), then enhance.

1. **Mobile** (default): single column, large touch targets, readable text, visible action bars.
2. **Tablet** (`min-width: 768px`): 2-column grids, more spacing, sidebar visible.
3. **Desktop**: `max-width` content containers, multi-column grids, generous padding.

Never write desktop-only CSS and patch mobile with `max-width` media queries.

## Breakpoints & tokens

- Primary breakpoint: **768px** (`--breakpoint-md` in `src/styles/tokens.scss`).
- Prefer `@media (min-width: 768px)` for desktop enhancements.
- Use theme CSS variables (`--primary`, `--background`, `--card`, `--border`, `--radius-*`) — no hardcoded colors except existing semantic badges.
- Full-height screens: `100dvh` (not `100vh` alone).
- iOS safe areas: `env(safe-area-inset-top)` / `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` on fixed headers and bottom bars.

## Responsive layout (established patterns)

### App shell (`layout.component`)

- Shell: `height: 100dvh; overflow: hidden`.
- Scrollable area: `flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow: auto` (`min-height: 0` is **required** on flex scroll children).
- Mobile: hidden sidebar, drawer menu (`mobile-menu`), reduced padding (`1.25rem 1rem`).
- Desktop: fixed sidebar, `margin-left: var(--sidebar-width)`.

### Immersive screens (e.g. cooking mode)

- Route **outside layout** in `app.routes.ts` to hide sidebar/topbar.
- Container: `height: 100dvh; max-height: 100dvh; overflow: hidden`.
- Header + action bar: `flex-shrink: 0`.
- Main content: only scrollable section (`min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto`).
- **Never** let long content push critical bottom action bars off-screen.

### Overlays & bottom sheets

- Overlay: `position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 40; background: rgb(0 0 0 / 50%)`.
- Panel: `position: fixed; z-index: 50`, bottom sheet `max-height: 70dvh`.
- `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal="true"` on modal panels.

## Touch targets & readability

- Primary action buttons: **min-height 48px** (52px for primary CTAs).
- `border-radius: var(--radius-pill)` for CTAs and filters.
- `:focus-visible` with `var(--ring)` outline on all interactive controls.
- Cooking/instruction text: `font-size ≥ 1.125rem`, `line-height: 1.6`, `white-space: pre-line`.

## Angular — structure & patterns

### Folder layout

```
features/<feature>/
  <feature>.component.ts|html|scss
  <feature>.routes.ts          # lazy load
  components/                  # feature sub-components
core/                          # services, models, guards, utils, mappers
shared/                        # cross-cutting components/services (alerts…)
layout/                        # shell, sidebar, topbar, mobile-menu
```

### Components

- **Standalone** only, explicit `imports` in decorator.
- Reactive state: **signals** + `computed()` — no BehaviorSubject for local UI state.
- Template fields/methods: `protected readonly`.
- Templates: native control flow `@if`, `@for`, `@else` — no `*ngIf`/`*ngFor`.
- Lazy loading via `loadComponent` in `*.routes.ts`.

### Imports

TypeScript aliases: `@core/*`, `@shared/*`, `@layout/*`, `@features/*`.

### Data

- Domain models in `core/models/`, API DTOs in `recipe-api.model.ts`.
- API → view mapping in `core/utils/*.mapper.ts`.
- Display formatting in `core/utils/recipe-format.util.ts`.
- Facade services: `RecipeDataService` — no direct HTTP calls from feature components.

### UI library

- PrimeNG for complex components (Dialog, Card, ProgressSpinner, Button…).
- Icons: PrimeIcons (`pi pi-*`).
- Global overrides in `src/styles/primeng-overrides.scss`.

## CSS conventions

- **BEM** with feature prefix: `.recipe-details__step-number`, `.cooking-mode__nav-btn--primary`.
- One SCSS file per component (`styleUrl`); shared styles in `src/styles/`.
- Responsive grids: `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(18rem, 1fr))`.
- Hero/detail: 1 column mobile → 2 columns at `768px`.
- Page containers: centered `max-width` (`56rem` detail, `75rem` library).

## Accessibility

- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons.
- `aria-live="polite"` for progress (e.g. step 2/6).
- `role="status"` on loading states.
- Images: descriptive `alt` attribute.

## UI delivery checklist

- [ ] Tested at 320px viewport — bottom buttons visible and tappable
- [ ] Long content scrolls without hiding fixed bars
- [ ] Safe areas respected on iPhone
- [ ] Styles use CSS tokens, no magic color values
- [ ] No desktop regression at 768px+
